{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem of finding the probability that exactly two of the dice show a 1 and exactly two of the dice show a 2 when six 6-sided dice are rolled, we will break down the problem step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the total number of possible outcomes\nEach die has 6 faces, so when rolling 6 dice, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n\\[\n6^6\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Determine the number of favorable outcomes\nWe need to count the number of ways to get exactly two 1's and exactly two 2's among the six dice. The remaining two dice can be any of the other four numbers (3, 4, 5, or 6).\n\n#### Step 2.1: Choose positions for the 1's and 2's\nFirst, we choose 2 positions out of 6 for the 1's. The number of ways to do this is given by the binomial coefficient:\n\\[\n\\binom{6}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we choose 2 positions out of the remaining 4 for the 2's. The number of ways to do this is:\n\\[\n\\binom{4}{2}\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":903,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,315,9271,279,18927,429,6896,1378,315,279,22120,1473,264,220,16,323,6896,1378,315,279,22120,1473,264,220,17,979,4743,220,21,49758,22120,525,22447,11,582,686,1438,1495,279,3491,3019,553,3019,382,14374,14822,220,16,25,29901,279,2790,1372,315,3204,19554,198,4854,2746,702,220,21,12300,11,773,979,20097,220,21,22120,11,279,2790,1372,315,3204,19554,374,510,59,9640,21,61,21,198,59,2533,14374,14822,220,17,25,29901,279,1372,315,36749,19554,198,1654,1184,311,1760,279,1372,315,5510,311,633,6896,1378,220,16,594,323,6896,1378,220,17,594,4221,279,4743,22120,13,576,9664,1378,22120,646,387,894,315,279,1008,3040,5109,320,18,11,220,19,11,220,20,11,476,220,21,3593,820,14822,220,17,13,16,25,22201,9892,369,279,220,16,594,323,220,17,594,198,5338,11,582,5157,220,17,9892,700,315,220,21,369,279,220,16,594,13,576,1372,315,5510,311,653,419,374,2661,553,